  "configuration_id": "config_017",
  "reason": "The evidence strongly points to scvi_n200 + transformer aggregation + weighted fusion as the best-performing combination (config_013: 0.725 acc, 3.60 GPU hrs). The only major untested design axis within this top-performing family is the image encoder: all five completed experiments used imagenet_vit_l. Config_017 (scvi_n200, resnet50, transformer, weighted, multiprofile, multimodal) directly tests whether resnet50 can match or approach the ViT-L performance while keeping the same aggregation and fusion. This is the highest-value uncertainty to resolve: if resnet50 is competitive, we gain a cheaper configuration; if it lags significantly, we confirm ViT-L is essential and can focus remaining budget on fine-tuning around the current best. Expected cost is moderate (~3–3.5 GPU hrs), slightly below config_013 since ResNet50 (~25M params) is much lighter than ViT-L (~307M params), making this a cost-efficient exploration of the image-encoder dimension with 4 experiments still remaining."
}

